module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.ZeroSchemeProperties
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjIdealSheaf.Basic

/-!
# The ideal of a closed subscheme of `Proj`, read on a standard chart

Let `S = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝒮 n` be a nonnegatively graded ring, `X = Proj 𝒮`, let `f ∈ 𝒮 d` be
homogeneous of positive degree, and let `i : Z ⟶ X` be a closed immersion. The standard open
`D₊(f)` is affine with ring of sections the degree-zero localization
`HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒮 f`, and the ideal cutting `Z` out of `X` there is
`Ker(Γ(X, D₊(f)) ⟶ Γ(Z, i⁻¹ D₊(f)))`.

This file relates that chart ideal to the homogeneous ideal
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.idealOfClosedSubscheme` of `Z`. The homogeneous
elements of `I(Z)` of degree `n * d` give, after division by `f ^ n`, elements of the chart
ring, and the result proved here is that every one of them lies in the chart ideal: the
degree-zero part of `I(Z)` localized at `f` is **contained in** `Ker(i.app D₊(f))`.

The mechanism is the local equation of a zero scheme. By the degreewise criterion of Tag 0BXK a
homogeneous `b` lies in `I(Z)` exactly when the canonical section of `𝒪(n d)` attached to it
pulls back to zero on `Z`, which by Tag 02OR says that the zero scheme of that section contains
`Z`, i.e. that its defining ideal on every affine open is carried to zero by `i`. On `D₊(f)` the
twisting sheaf is trivialized by `f ^ n`, so that defining ideal is *principal*, generated by the
single chart function `b / f ^ n` — which is therefore in the kernel.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheafModule`: the twisting sheaf `𝒪(m)`
  with its type declared at `(Proj 𝒮).Modules`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistTrivialization`: the trivialization of
  `𝒪(n d)` over `D₊(f)`, at the spelling the zero scheme consumes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.chartFraction`: the chart function `b / f ^ n`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistTrivialization_restrict_degreeSection`: the
  trivialization carries the canonical section of `b` to `b / f ^ n`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.zeroScheme_degreeSection_ideal_basicOpen`: **the
  local equation on a standard chart** — the defining ideal of the zero scheme of the canonical
  section of `b` over `D₊(f)` is generated by `b / f ^ n`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj`
  `.chartFraction_mem_ker_app_of_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme`: **the containment**
  `I(Z)₍f₎ ≤ Ker(i.app D₊(f))`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.projectiveSpace_chartFraction_mem_ker_app`: the same
  on projective space, where the invertibility hypotheses are instances.

## Implementation notes

Three spelling crossings are made once each, and none of them needs a transparency lever.

`twistingSheaf 𝒮 m` is a `SheafOfModules` over `sheafCompose … (structureSheaf 𝒮)` while
`AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme` consumes `(Proj 𝒮).Modules`. The two agree definitionally but the
`Γ(L, U)` notation cannot elaborate the first spelling, and instantiating
`AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization` at it directly exhausts the elaborator's
budget on a single `isDefEq`. The cure is `twistingSheafModule`, a `noncomputable abbrev` whose
*declared type* is `(Proj 𝒮).Modules`; with the trivialization restated at that spelling the
instantiation is immediate.

The trivialization `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization.trivializingEquiv` is indexed by
an integer `n` and lands in degree `n * d`, whereas `degreeSection` is indexed by a natural
number and lands in degree `((n * d : ℕ) : ℤ)`. These are equal but not syntactically so. The
transport is performed once, in `twistTrivialization`, and `twistTrivialization_apply` discharges
it by `subst` in a statement where the degree is a *variable* — the fibres of the sheaf do not
mention the degree, so the pointwise formula is transport-free.

`Localization.mk` and `LocalizedModule.mk` agree here because `Localization P` and
`LocalizedModule P S` are the same type, as
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjTrivialization/Basic.lean` records; the arithmetic is
therefore a single `Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff`.

The containment proved here is one half of Tag 0801's chart comparison. The reverse inclusion —
every element of `Ker(i.app D₊(f))` is `b / f ^ n` for some `b ∈ I(Z)` — is **not** proved here:
it needs, besides this file, that an inequality of ideal sheaves may be checked on the
standard-open cover, that `Ker(i.app ·)` localizes along `D₊(f g) ⊆ D₊(f)`, and the resulting
`f`-power saturation, so it is a separate piece of work. Accordingly no `@[stacks 0801]`
attribute is attached: the tag asserts the equality.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0801](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0801)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj

open AlgebraicGeometry

universe u w

variable {S : Type u} [CommRing S] {σ : Type w} [SetLike σ S] [AddSubgroupClass σ S]
  (𝒮 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒮]

attribute [local implicit_reducible] TopCat.Sheaf sheafCompose
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf
attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top

variable {f : S} {d : ℕ}

/-- The twisting sheaf `𝒪_{Proj 𝒮}(m)`, with its type declared at `(Proj 𝒮).Modules`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf` and nothing more; the point of
the `abbrev` is the declared type. `twistingSheaf 𝒮 m` is a `SheafOfModules` over
`sheafCompose … (structureSheaf 𝒮)`, which is definitionally `(Proj 𝒮).ringCatSheaf` but is not
accepted by the `Γ(L, U)` notation and makes `AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme`'s trivialization
argument prohibitively expensive to unify. -/
abbrev twistingSheafModule (m : ℤ) : (Proj 𝒮).Modules := twistingSheaf 𝒮 m

/-- The degree of `f ^ n` for `f` of degree `d`, as an integer: `n • d` and `n * d` agree. -/
theorem natCast_nsmul_eq_mul (n d : ℕ) : ((n • d : ℕ) : ℤ) = (n : ℤ) * (d : ℤ) := by
  simp [smul_eq_mul]

/-- **The trivialization of `𝒪(n d)` over `D₊(f)`**, in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization` consumes: a linear equivalence of the
sections of the twist with the sections of the structure sheaf, over the ring of sections of the
structure sheaf.

This is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization.trivializingEquiv` with the degree rewritten
from `(n : ℤ) * d` to `((n • d : ℕ) : ℤ)` and the direction reversed. -/
def twistTrivialization (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 d) (n : ℕ) :
    Γ(twistingSheafModule 𝒮 ((n • d : ℕ) : ℤ), Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f)
      ≃ₗ[Γ(Proj 𝒮, Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f)] Γ(Proj 𝒮, Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f) :=
  ((natCast_nsmul_eq_mul n d) ▸
    trivializingEquiv 𝒮 hf (n : ℤ) (le_refl (ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f))).symm

/-- The pointwise formula for the inverse of `twistTrivialization`: it is multiplication by the
trivializing value `f ^ n`.

The degree is a variable here, so the transport performed in `twistTrivialization` is discharged
by `subst` and the statement is about
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization.trivializingHom`, whose pointwise formula is
definitional. -/
theorem twistTrivialization_apply (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 d) (n : ℕ) {m : ℤ} (hm : (n : ℤ) * (d : ℤ) = m)
    (a : Γ(Proj 𝒮, Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f)) (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f) :
    ((hm ▸ trivializingEquiv 𝒮 hf (n : ℤ) (le_refl (ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f))) a
        : moduleSections 𝒮 (twistGrading (S := S) 𝒮 m) (ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f)).1 x
      = HomogeneousLocalization.val (a.1 x) * trivializingFun 𝒮 (n : ℤ) le_rfl x := by
  subst hm
  rfl

/-- The chart function `b / f ^ n` attached to a homogeneous element `b` of degree `n * d`: a
section of the structure sheaf over the standard open `D₊(f)`. -/
def chartFraction (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 d) (n : ℕ) (b : 𝒮 (n • d)) : Γ(Proj 𝒮, Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f) :=
  (Proj.awayToSection 𝒮 f).hom (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒮 hf n (b : S) b.2)

/-- The value of the chart function `b / f ^ n` in the local ring at a point of `D₊(f)`. -/
theorem val_chartFraction_apply (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 d) (n : ℕ) (b : 𝒮 (n • d))
    (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.val ((chartFraction 𝒮 hf n b).1 x)
      = Localization.mk (b : S)
          ⟨f ^ n, x.1.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl.pow_mem x.2 n⟩ := by
  refine (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.awayToSection_apply 𝒮 f _ x).trans ?_
  rw [HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk, Localization.mk_eq_mk', IsLocalization.map_mk',
    ← Localization.mk_eq_mk']
  rfl

/-- Multiplying the fraction `b / f ^ n` by the trivializing value `f ^ n` gives `b / 1`. -/
theorem mk_mul_trivializingFun (n : ℕ) (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f) (b : S) :
    Localization.mk b ⟨f ^ n, x.1.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl.pow_mem x.2 n⟩
        * trivializingFun 𝒮 (n : ℤ) (le_refl (ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f)) x
      = Localization.mk b (1 : x.1.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl) := by
  rw [trivializingFun, Localization.mk_mul]
  refine Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff.mpr (Localization.r_of_eq ?_)
  simp [Int.toNat_natCast]
  ring

/-- The value at a point of `D₊(f)` of the restriction of the canonical section of `𝒪(k)`
attached to a homogeneous element `b` of degree `k`: it is `b / 1`. -/
theorem restrict_degreeSection_apply (k : ℕ) (b : 𝒮 k)
    (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f) :
    ((twistingSheafModule 𝒮 (k : ℤ)).presheaf.map
          (homOfLE (le_top : Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f ≤ ⊤)).op (degreeSection 𝒮 k b)).1 x
      = LocalizedModule.mk (b : S) (1 : x.1.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl) :=
  associatedModuleSheaf_restrict_apply (𝒜 := 𝒮) (𝒨 := twistGrading (S := S) 𝒮 (k : ℤ))
    (homOfLE (le_top : ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f ≤ ⊤)) (degreeSection 𝒮 k b) x

/-- **The trivialization carries the canonical section of `b` to the chart function `b / f ^ n`.**
Both sides are computed in the fibre over each point of `D₊(f)`, where the statement is the
cancellation `(b / f ^ n) · f ^ n = b / 1`. -/
theorem twistTrivialization_restrict_degreeSection (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 d) (n : ℕ) (b : 𝒮 (n • d)) :
    twistTrivialization 𝒮 hf n
        ((twistingSheafModule 𝒮 ((n • d : ℕ) : ℤ)).presheaf.map
          (homOfLE (le_top : Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f ≤ ⊤)).op (degreeSection 𝒮 (n • d) b))
      = chartFraction 𝒮 hf n b := by
  refine (LinearEquiv.symm_apply_eq _).mpr (Subtype.ext (funext fun x => ?_))
  refine Eq.symm ((twistTrivialization_apply 𝒮 hf n (natCast_nsmul_eq_mul n d).symm
    (chartFraction 𝒮 hf n b) x).trans ?_)
  rw [val_chartFraction_apply 𝒮 hf n b x, mk_mul_trivializingFun 𝒮 n x (b : S)]
  exact (restrict_degreeSection_apply 𝒮 (n • d) b x).symm

/-- **The local equation of the zero scheme of a canonical twisted section on a standard chart.**
The defining ideal, over `D₊(f)`, of the zero scheme of the section of `𝒪(n d)` attached to a
homogeneous element `b` of degree `n * d` is generated by the single chart function `b / f ^ n`.

This is Tag 02OR's local principality, with the explicit trivialization of Tag 01MS supplying the
generator. -/
theorem zeroScheme_degreeSection_ideal_basicOpen (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 d) (hd : 0 < d) (n : ℕ)
    (b : 𝒮 (n • d))
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (Proj 𝒮).sheaf.obj (Proj 𝒮).ringCatSheaf.property
      (twistingSheafModule 𝒮 ((n • d : ℕ) : ℤ))] :
    (zeroScheme (Proj 𝒮) (twistingSheafModule 𝒮 ((n • d : ℕ) : ℤ))
          (degreeSection 𝒮 (n • d) b)).ideal
        ⟨Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f, Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒮 f hf hd⟩
      = Ideal.span {chartFraction 𝒮 hf n b} :=
  zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization (Proj 𝒮) (twistingSheafModule 𝒮 ((n • d : ℕ) : ℤ))
    (degreeSection 𝒮 (n • d) b) ⟨Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f, Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒮 f hf hd⟩
    (twistTrivialization 𝒮 hf n) (chartFraction 𝒮 hf n b)
    (twistTrivialization_restrict_degreeSection 𝒮 hf n b)

/-- **The degree-zero part of `I(Z)` localized at `f` is contained in `Ker(i.app D₊(f))`.**

If a homogeneous element `b` of degree `n * d` lies in the homogeneous ideal of a closed
subscheme `Z ⊆ Proj 𝒮`, then the chart function `b / f ^ n` is carried to zero by `i` over the
standard open `D₊(f)`.

This is one inclusion of Tag 0801's chart comparison; see the module docstring for what the
reverse inclusion still needs. -/
theorem chartFraction_mem_ker_app_of_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 d) (hd : 0 < d)
    {Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Proj 𝒮) [IsClosedImmersion i] (n : ℕ) (b : 𝒮 (n • d))
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (Proj 𝒮).sheaf.obj (Proj 𝒮).ringCatSheaf.property
      (twistingSheafModule 𝒮 ((n • d : ℕ) : ℤ))]
    (hb : (b : S) ∈ idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 i) :
    chartFraction 𝒮 hf n b ∈ RingHom.ker (i.app (Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f)).hom := by
  have hdec : (DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 (b : S) (n • d) : 𝒮 (n • d)) = b :=
    Subtype.ext (DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒮 b.2)
  have hzero : pullbackGlobalSections i (twistingSheaf 𝒮 ((n • d : ℕ) : ℤ))
      (degreeSection 𝒮 (n • d) b) = 0 := by
    have h := (mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_iff 𝒮 i (b : S)).mp hb (n • d)
    rwa [hdec] at h
  have hle : zeroScheme (Proj 𝒮) (twistingSheafModule 𝒮 ((n • d : ℕ) : ℤ))
      (degreeSection 𝒮 (n • d) b) ≤ i.ker :=
    (pullbackGlobalSections_degreeSection_eq_zero_iff_zeroScheme_le_ker 𝒮 i b).mp hzero
  have hideal := Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_ofIdeals_iff.mp hle
    ⟨Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f, Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒮 f hf hd⟩
  rw [zeroScheme_degreeSection_ideal_basicOpen 𝒮 hf hd n b] at hideal
  exact hideal (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)

section ProjectiveSpace

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (e : ℕ)

/-- **The chart containment on projective space.** A homogeneous polynomial of degree `n` lying in
the homogeneous ideal of a closed subscheme `Z ⊆ P^{e-1}_R` gives, after division by `X k ^ n`, an
element of the kernel of `i` over the standard chart `D₊(X k)`.

The two invertibility hypotheses of the general statement are instances here, a polynomial ring
being generated in degree one. -/
theorem projectiveSpace_chartFraction_mem_ker_app {Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (i : Z ⟶ Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin e) R)) [IsClosedImmersion i]
    (k : Fin e) (n : ℕ)
    (b : MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin e) R (n • 1))
    (hb : (b : MvPolynomial (Fin e) R) ∈
      idealOfClosedSubscheme (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin e) R) i) :
    chartFraction (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin e) R)
        (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_X R k) n b ∈
      RingHom.ker (i.app (Proj.basicOpen (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin e) R)
        (MvPolynomial.X k))).hom :=
  chartFraction_mem_ker_app_of_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme _
    (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_X R k) one_pos i n b hb

end ProjectiveSpace

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj

end
